        "original_id": "87aa4401-79d6-5624-8871-e508fc65b9da",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Willem van Oldenbarnevelt, Johan van Oldenbarnevelt\n- Roles: Lord of Stoutenburg, Lord of Berkel en Rodenrijs, Lord of Gunterstein, Lord of Bakkum, Dutch statesman\n- Places: Stoutenburg, Berkel en Rodenrijs, Gunterstein, Bakkum, Spain\n- Topics: Dutch struggle for independence\n\nFacts:\n- Johan van Oldenbarnevelt was born on 14 September 1547.\n- Johan van Oldenbarnevelt became Lord of Berkel en Rodenrijs in 1600.\n- Johan van Oldenbarnevelt became Lord of Gunterstein in 1611.\n- Johan van Oldenbarnevelt became Lord of Bakkum in 1613.\n- Johan van Oldenbarnevelt was a Dutch statesman who played an important role in the Dutch struggle for independence from Spain.\n- Johan van Oldenbarnevelt died on 13 May 1619.\n- Willem van Oldenbarnevelt was born in 1590.\n- Willem van Oldenbarnevelt held the title Lord of Stoutenburg.\n- Willem van Oldenbarnevelt was a son of Johan van Oldenbarnevelt.\n- Willem van Oldenbarnevelt died before 1638.",
